{"clean": true, "issues": [], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-14 (structure only; the runtime check belongs to the look workflow)", "what": "Static count of visual mesh nodes (MeshInstance3D + CSG) that Map 01 brings into the main scene, per sub-scene", "value": "Terrain 3 (Island and CanyonRoad are CSG, plus SaltFlat), Water 3, Cliffs 5 CSG, Fords 2, each Base 18 visible + 1 hidden Pad + 2 Flag meshes, Cover 12, Depot 20 ring dashes + 3 tanks + 5 Cans x 3, 4 outer Cans x 3. About 115 visible instances, roughly 250 draw calls for both views at the look preflight's 2.2 per instance, against the 1,000 budget. Runtime draw calls were not measured here.", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "G-3 look-readiness", "what": "Scaled MeshInstance3D/CSG nodes; meshes or CSG nodes without a material file under maps/map_01/materials; colour literals in Map scenes; ground surfaces that cast shadows; identical props that do not share one mesh", "value": "0 / 0 / 0 (the only colours are the Environment's sky and ambient, copied from the greybox per G-2) / 0 / 0", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-9 (structure)", "what": "Map contract and composition typing: MapField exports, the type of SplitScreen.field, and code typed GreyboxField that could run on Map 01", "value": "MapField exports player_1_base, player_2_base and token_stock. SplitScreen.field is typed MapField and reads only the two Bases. GreyboxField is used only in greybox code: driving_toy.gd, layout.gd, bases.gd and the runner's swap.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-5 (structure)", "what": "Ford and Unit.limit_speed: type names in code, zone layer/mask, monitoring toggles, body_entered handlers, number of FordSettings resources", "value": "0 type names; layer 0, mask 2 (the Gyrocopter on 16 is never listed); 0 toggles; 0 handlers; 1 shared ford_settings.tres (0.5); _yaw_rate untouched", "verdict": "PASS"}], "checked": "Architecture review, read-only. I did not run Godot. Files read: story 007 in full, story 008, EPIC.md; map_field.gd, token_stock.gd, ford.gd, ford_settings.gd, ford.tscn, data/ford_settings.tres, data/token_stock.tres; map_01.tscn and its five sub-scenes; compound_base.tscn; all 16 materials/*.tres; the diffs of unit.gd, split_screen.gd, split_screen.tscn, greybox_field.gd, split_screen_harness.gd, design/rules.md and the class cache; base.gd in full; the structure of map_kit.gd; the composition, script-list and mirror parts of map_layout.gd. The map_* scenarios contain no private member access, set_drive_input, Timer, monitoring toggle or carry_by call. I found nothing that forces a rewrite of this story's files for the look workflow, story 008 or a later Map.\n\n(1) MapField and SplitScreen are sound. MapField is data only: three exports. GreyboxField extends it, and greybox_field.tscn is untouched. Story 008 can pass field.token_stock to begin() from SplitScreen._ready(). The runner already gives the greybox field the same token_stock.tres, so story 008 reads the stock from either composition. TokenStock's typed counts and count_of(type_id) match the type ids in UnitStats.\n\n(2) The greybox swap is honest. Its class doc says what it swaps. It puts back exactly the three nodes the old split_screen.tscn had (no overrides), with the same names and at World indices 0 to 2. It frees the Map with remove_child() and free() and points split.field at the greybox field. Low-priority fragilities:\n- It finds the nodes by the literal names \"World\" and \"Map\". Freeing root.field and using its parent would survive a rename.\n- GREYBOX_SCENARIOS is keyed by name, like LEGACY_SCENARIOS. Story 008's rename of canister_run and canister_showcase must rename those entries too. A miss fails loudly on Map 01.\n- If the look workflow recolours the Units in split_screen.tscn, it must undo that in this helper, as C-5 already says.\n- The runner's wall_clearance_min uses FIELD_HALF_EXTENT 40, so it only means something on the greybox. No Map 01 scenario reads it, but its doc could say so.\n\n(3) The sub-scene split and names are clear and leave room for the look's dressing:\n- Terrain: Island CSG, SaltFlat, CanyonRoad CSG, ShoreEdge with 32 bodies\n- Water: Sea and two channels\n- Cliffs: five CSG nodes\n- FordWest and FordEast, Base1 and Base2, Cover, Depot, and the four named outer Cans\nThe Map is World's child 0, so the Fords tick before the Units, and map_layout asserts this.\n\n(4) The shared material files reach every Map surface. Every mesh and CSG node references one file, no node is scaled, ground surfaces cast no shadow, props share meshes, and the overlay heights match G-3(b). By design, the Team colour reaches the Bases another way: two color_material ext_resource lines in map_01.tscn that point at split_screen/data/player_*_body_material.tres. The Flag and the Fuel Can are their own scenes. Notes for the look workflow:\n- The corner towers share BoxMesh_corner_tower and wall.tres across both Bases. Their Team colour needs the per-instance path the story names (a list on Base or the team_colour group).\n- The Garage walls use wall.tres.\n- ford.tscn is a generic scene under maps/ but references map_01/materials/ford.tres, so a later Map's fords would look like Map 01's unless overridden.\n- Rock and water share layer 32, and the channel bodies are 1.5 m tall. The Gyrocopter's visual rise over rock must tell rock from water by node or group, not by layer.\n\n(5) Ford and limit_speed: the fraction is data, no Unit type is named, the Gyrocopter is excluded by the mask, the zone is polled, Units that are not alive are skipped, and the cap lapses by frame stamp. One API remark: within a tick the last caller wins, not the lowest fraction. That is fine with Map 01's separate fords; if a later Map has overlapping slow zones, take the lower fraction in that tick.\n\n(6) The compound Base on base.gd: the hidden Pad (a footprint for first_spawn_problem()) and the Tank used as beacon are what the story itself prescribes, not hacks. GarageQueue, CanisterRules and MatchController read only spawn_point, the spares, zone, canister and canister_seat, so story 008's Garage spawn works unchanged. Story 008's Flag rename must also edit, mechanically:\n- compound_base.tscn: node_paths canister and canister_seat, the nodes Canister and CanisterSeat, and the path to water_canister.tscn (path-only references are the project's convention)\n- map_layout: the SCRIPTS list and \"Base1/CanisterSeat\"\n- map_kit and map_bases: canister_seat and WaterCanister.State\nA miss fails loudly at begin().\nbase.gd's docs still describe only base.tscn: a pillar beacon, the seat 4.5 m behind the spawn point, \"not an obstacle\". base.gd is outside this workflow's file list. The look workflow edits base.gd for the Team-colour list, so it should update those docs to cover both scenes.\nThe compound's camera-height limits (B-4) and the U-turn strip outside each gate (D-3) are recorded only in the preflight and evidence doc, and no scenario checks line of sight. The look's dressing must respect them; AC-13 is checked there.\n\n(7) unit.gd at 687 to 735 lines and the scenario sizes are covered by the orchestrator's rulings. Step 6 is documented in the movement model.\n\n(8) The depot ring is 20 dash nodes, not DESIGN 5.8's single thin cylinder or torus. All of them share one mesh and one material, so it is cheap. This is a fidelity note for the orchestrator, not rework."}
