on against A-1", "value": "32 of 32 bodies match to under 1e-5 m; island polygon is A-1's 32 vertices; canyon and ridge polygons are mirror-symmetric", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "STD docs", "what": "Docs citing measurements or sources without the 'the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run' pointer", "value": "preflight or correction-id citations and unretained measured numbers in map_edges.gd (about 12), map_bases.gd (5), map_ford.gd (3), map_kit.gd (5), map_layout.gd (2); ford.gd cites a Story 006 doc that lacks the probe", "verdict": "FAIL"}, {"ac": "STD docs", "what": "Private-function doc density in the new scenarios against the Story 002 to 006 scenarios", "value": "map_layout 6/20, map_kit 1/9 (kit precedent is looser); map_edges, map_ford, map_bases and map_cover 100%, as are all older scenarios", "verdict": "FAIL"}, {"ac": "STD vocab", "what": "Garage/Flag/Fuel Can vocabulary, scenario or check names in src docs, debug prints, tools/ references from src, player-facing strings in src", "value": "no 'pad' or 'spawn point' used for the Garage in any new text; no scenario or check name in any src doc; 0 prints in src; the only tools/ mention in src is a pre-existing unit.gd line outside the diff; new src strings are push_error developer messages only", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-5", "what": "Ford code against the DESIGN and corrections C-1/C-2: poll once per tick, no body_entered, no monitoring toggle, no group, no type check, settings validated in _ready(), data in .tres", "value": "matches; ford_settings.tres speed_fraction 0.5 shared by both fords; token_stock.tres in the exact C-4 form", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "regress", "what": "Byte-identical strict twenty, soft four, five new scenarios (twice), launch checks, seeded-defect proofs", "value": "not run: this lens may not run Godot", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "I read every file the story added or changed: the four new src scripts and their .tres and ford.tscn, the unit.gd, split_screen.g