{"clean": true, "issues": [], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-9 / DESIGN 3.1 (Map contract)", "what": "How SplitScreen, the Map, GreyboxField and the Map 01 scenarios use the field", "value": "split_screen.gd:108 types field as MapField and reads only player_1_base and player_2_base. map_01.tscn root Map uses map_field.gd with player_1_base=Base1, player_2_base=Base2, token_stock=data/token_stock.tres. GreyboxField extends MapField and greybox_field.tscn is unchanged. map_kit.gd types the field as MapField. Only the greybox scenarios layout.gd and bases.gd and the frozen driving toy read player_start or type the field as GreyboxField.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-9 / C-4 (TokenStock)", "what": "TokenStock form, and whether its keys match the Unit data story 008 reads", "value": "Dictionary[StringName, int] with count_of() returning 0 for an unknown id. The .tres is in ResourceSaver form: motorbike 5, buggy 3, truck 2, gyrocopter 2. Every *_stats.tres carries the matching type_id.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-5 / C-1 / C-2 (Ford API)", "what": "Ford and Unit.limit_speed: data, type names, Gyrocopter exclusion, tree order", "value": "ford.tscn: layer 0, mask 2, BoxShape3D 12x3x40 at y 1.5, one shared ford_settings.tres (0.5). Polled through get_overlapping_bodies() with an is_alive guard; no body_entered, no monitoring toggle, no type names. The cap is clamped only while the frame stamp is at most 1 tick old; _yaw_rate is untouched. The Map is World's first child so the Fords tick before the Units; ford.gd and split_screen.gd document this.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-14 structure / G-3(d) (draw-call footprint)", "what": "MeshInstance3D and CSG nodes per sub-scene", "value": "terrain: 1 MeshInstance3D + 2 CSG (32 shore bodies have no mesh). water: 3 (sea 1000x1000, 2 channel surfaces on one PlaneMesh). cliffs: 5 CSG. ford: 1 each, 2 total. compound_base: 19 each, 38 total, 36 visible; both Bases share its 10 mesh resources. cover: 12 on 3 shared BoxMeshes. depot: 23 (20 ring dashes on 1 PlaneMesh, 3 tanks on 1 CylinderMesh) + 5 Cans. Fuel Cans: 9 x 3 = 27. Flags: 2 x 2 = 4. Total about 115 visible drawables. The look preflight's ceiling is about 446 separate-mesh instances for 1,000 draw calls, and its 58-mesh mock cost 147.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "G-3 (a)(b)(c)(f) / DESIGN 5.0 (look-readiness)", "what": "Node scaling, where colours live, ground shadows and overlay heights, read from the scene text", "value": "0 node-scaled transforms in 9 scenes. Every Map 01 mesh and CSG material is an ExtResource under map_01/materials (16 files); 0 StandardMaterial3D sub_resources and 0 material_override lines in the Map scenes. cast_shadow is 0 on island, road, salt flat, sea, channels, fords, Garage floor, pad and the 20 ring dashes. Surface tops: island 0.002, salt flat and road 0.010, ford, channel and ring 0.020, Garage floor 0.030, sea -0.12.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "DESIGN 3.3 / C-5 (greybox composition)", "what": "Whether the runner's swap matches what split_screen.tscn lost", "value": "The split_screen.tscn diff removes only GreyboxField, TerrainStandIns and FuelCans, and they had no overrides besides unique_name_in_owner. It adds Map with field=%Map. _apply_greybox_composition runs after instantiate() and before add_child(). It frees the Map with remove_child()+free() before it enters the tree, so its Cans never join fuel_cans. It restores the three nodes at indices 0..2 with their names, unique name, owner and token_stock, and reassigns split.field. GREYBOX_SCENARIOS has 21 names, including fps.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "DESIGN 5.0 (shared data at runtime)", "what": "Runtime writes to the shared material or data resources", "value": "grep over src/gameplay for albedo_color writes and duplicate(): none. Base paints only through material_override. Ford and TokenStock are read-only.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "TD-010 / TD-006 (rulings)", "what": "File sizes", "value": "unit.gd 735 (+48), map_kit 319, map_layout 349, map_edges 452, map_bases 295, map_cover 301, map_ford 281: all inside the orchestrator's rulings", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "Story 008 forward risk (DESIGN 3.3)", "what": "How many Units the older greybox scenarios spend, against the example stock the runner now gives them", "value": "The strict destruction baseline prints unit_destroyed=18/4. respawn_showcase, countdown, units_showcase and fuel_showcase also destroy and respawn repeatedly. The greybox stock is Motorbike 5, Gyrocopter 2. Once story 008 charges a Token per destruction and ends the Round at 0 Motorbike Tokens, these outputs change unless story 008 gives GREYBOX_SCENARIOS a larger stock in _apply_greybox_composition (a few lines in this story's runner).", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "Architecture review only. I did not run Godot (my role); regress, launch and import results belong to the other lenses.\n\nI read:\n- the change set (git status and diff of greybox_field.gd, split_screen.gd/.tscn, unit.gd, split_screen_harness.gd, the class cache, rules.md);\n- every new game file in full: map_field.gd, token_stock.gd, ford.gd, ford_settings.gd, ford.tscn, both data .tres, map_01.tscn, compound_base.tscn and the 16 materials;\n- the terrain, water, cliffs, depot and cover scenes, by script summary and spot reads;\n- base.gd, map_kit.gd (outline), and a grep of the five map_* scenarios for node paths and private-member access (none found);\n- story 007 (including AC-10 to AC-15), story 008, EPIC.md and the look preflight report.\n\n**Verdict:** no issue costs real rework or breaks something. The structure is a sound base for the look workflow, story 008 and later Maps.\n\n**Look workflow**\n- It reaches every Map 01 mesh through one material file per surface kind. The CSG nodes take their material the same way.\n- The exceptions are by design:\n  - Fuel Cans: materials embedded in fuel_can.tscn.\n  - Flags: water_canister.tscn plus color_material.\n  - Tank: the beacon, painted with color_material at runtime.\n  - Corner towers: wall.tres. Their Team colour needs the base.gd edit the story's \"Base paint\" note already plans: a persistent team_colour group on the four Walls/Tower*/Mesh nodes, or an exported array. No geometry change.\n- The PlaneMesh and CSG cap UVs run 0..1 over each mesh. World-metre tiling therefore needs uv1_scale per file or uv1_world_triplanar. Each file serves one mesh size, so this is a material-file edit only.\n- The look preflight's sand-tinted Base floor would be a new mesh at y 0.010; the height ladder has room for it.\n- The sea is \u00b1500 m. G-3 requires at least \u00b1400; the preflight measured \u00b1700 as seam-free. Widening it is one number in map_01_water.tscn.\n- Rock and channel water share layer 32. The Gyrocopter's visual rise over rock cannot tell rock from water by layer, but it can by a group or node type (small edit).\n- Orange and Teal Units in split_screen.tscn will need blue and red restored in _apply_greybox_composition, as C-5 already notes. Every presentation edit to split_screen.tscn has to be mirrored there the same way. The World/Map node names are hard-coded in the helper.\n\n**Story 008**\n- SplitScreen can hand field.token_stock to begin(). count_of() is keyed by UnitStats.type_id. The driving toy keeps a field with no stock and no Round.\n- The Flag rename will also touch:\n  - compound_base.tscn: the canister and canister_seat node_paths, and the Canister/CanisterSeat node names.\n  - map_layout.gd: the SCRIPTS entry water_canister.gd and the Base1/CanisterSeat table entry.\n  - GREYBOX_SCENARIOS: canister_run and canister_showcase. A name missing from that list runs on Map 01.\n- Forward risk: the example stock on the greybox composition versus destruction's 18 destructions (see measurements). No fix is proposed because DESIGN 3.3 names that stock.\n\n**Later Maps**\n- MapField, TokenStock and compound_base.tscn are reusable.\n- ford.tscn is a generic scene that hard-references map_01/materials/ford.tres, the shared ford_settings.tres and a fixed 12 x 40 m size. That is fine for v0.1; a later Map overrides these per instance or gets its own scene.\n\n**Lower-priority remarks**\n- base.gd's docs, which were not edited and are outside DESIGN's file list, still describe base.tscn: a 12 x 12 pad, a pillar beacon, and the seat 4.5 m behind the spawn point inside the pad. compound_base.tscn differs: a hidden 12 x 10 pad, the tank as beacon, and the seat 12 m ahead of the SpawnPoint and outside the pad. Nothing enforces those claims (first_spawn_problem checks spawn points only). The look's base.gd edit is the moment to fix the doc.\n- The Map node in split_screen.tscn has no unique_id. This is cosmetic; the editor adds one on its next save.\n- The redundant unique_name_in_owner on map_01.tscn's root is harmless.\n- After this story, the Story 002\u2013006 behaviours (HUD, countdown, Round-over, choice, weapons, Fuel) are proven only on the rebuilt greybox composition. Map 01 is covered by the five map_* scenarios and the launch check. This is the accepted trade-off of DESIGN 3.3, and story 008's new scenarios run on Map 01 by default.\n- The class cache diff (4 new classes, GreyboxField based on MapField) is consistent.\n- The latest run-out files of the soft four match the baseline byte sizes (sizes only, not diffed by me)."}
