{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "FIDELITY", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01_water.tscn", "quote": "[sub_resource type=\"PlaneMesh\" id=\"PlaneMesh_channel\"]\nmaterial = ExtResource(\"2_channel\")\nsize = Vector2(12, 28)   (each Surface at local (0, 0.02, 0) under ChannelWest/ChannelEast at Z 34, so it spans Z 20..48)", "problem": "Correction B-2 is binding: the channels' 'visual surfaces stop at the shoreline or continue in the sea's material'. At X 34..46 the A-1 shoreline sits at Z 45.99..46.07. Each channel surface therefore runs about 1.9 m past it, lying on the sea in channel.tres, which is a separate file from sea.tres. Today it is invisible: both files hold albedo Color(0.28, 0.5, 0.62), and the L3b capture shows the channels merging into the sea. But the look workflow re-textures by editing material files only (G-3, no geometry rework). If channel.tres ever stops matching the sea, two 12 x 1.9 m channel-coloured strips will show on the sea past the south shore, and fixing them would need a geometry edit. Only the visual plane is affected: the collision boxes reaching Z 48 are an accepted ruling.", "fix": "Stop the two surfaces at the shoreline and leave the collision boxes as they are: set PlaneMesh_channel size = Vector2(12, 26) and set both ChannelWest/Surface and ChannelEast/Surface transform origins to (0, 0.02, -1), so the surfaces span Z 20..46. Alternative: the orchestrator records that the surfaces run on past the shore and that channel.tres must keep matching sea.tres."}, {"kind": "FIDELITY", "file": "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_01/compound_base.tscn", "quote": "[sub_resource type=\"BoxShape3D\" id=\"BoxShape3D_leg\"]\nsize = Vector3(0.6, 8, 0.6)", "problem": "The story file and the design block disagree here. The story's Implementation Notes (Collision layers) list 'the tower legs' among the layer-1 bodies and require 'every layer-1 wall is built from boxes at least 1 m thick (unit.gd: walls must be at least 1 m thick)'. DESIGN 5.6 and correction D-1 bind 0.6 m square legs, and the build follows the design. The design block says such a difference is 'a finding for the orchestrator'. It is physically harmless: A-6 and B-6 measured no tunnelling through walls 0.02 to 2 m thick at top speed, and D-1/D-2 measured the exits with 0.6 m legs.", "fix": "No geometry change. Thickening the legs to 1 m would cut the measured lane clearances (Truck 0.5 m to the legs) to 0.3 m and invalidate the D-1/D-2 runs. Record in the Story 007 evidence doc that each Base's four water-tower legs are 0.6 m posts under the story's 1 m wall rule, citing A-6."}, {"kind": "UNVERIFIED", "file": "/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/lens-fidelity/top.png", "quote": "godot --path ... --windowed --resolution 2640x800 -s .../tools/topdown.gd -- --scene=res://src/gameplay/maps/map_01/map_01.tscn --out=.../lens-fidelity/top.png --width=330", "problem": "This is a coverage gap, not a build defect. The session's tools were only Read/Glob/Grep/Write/Edit, with no shell, so this lens could not run Godot or Python. It took no top-down snapshot of its own and ran no scripted transform parse. Every position and mirror number below was computed by hand from the current .tscn text. The visual comparison used the implementers' slice captures (impl/L3b/top_full.png, impl/L3b/top_depot.png, impl/L3a/top_base1.png, impl/L2b/top_canyon.png). Every number I checked against them agrees with the current scene files, but they were taken before any later fix round.", "fix": "Either re-run the TOP-DOWN SNAPSHOT command from a session with a shell (whole Map at --width=330, plus --cx=-120 --width=40 and --cx=120 --width=40), or accept the L3a/L3b captures as this lens's visual record."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-1", "what": "Island outline (Terrain/Island polygon) vs correction A-1 and vs the story table", "value": "Matches the 32-vertex A-1 list exactly. Moves from the table: 0.1 m at (0,\u00b146), 0.9 m at (\u00b130,\u00b147), 0.9 m at (\u00b160,\u00b145), 0.3 m at (\u00b190,\u00b146); every other vertex 0. Slab spans y -0.198..0.002, no collision", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1", "what": "Base A/B compound, Base-local converted to world (Base1: X=-120-z, Z=x; Base2: X=120+z, Z=-x)", "value": "Outer wall faces X -135..-105, Z -16..16 (0 m). Gate Z -5.5..5.5 against the table's -5..5 (0.5 m, D-1). Garage X -132..-122, Z -6..6 (0). SpawnPoint (-125,0) and spares (-125,\u00b14), facing +X (Base B -X) (0). Flag seat and tank centre (-113,0), tank 8 m across, bottom at y 8 (0). Zone X -133.6..-106.1, Z \u00b114.7 (0). Corner towers 4.3 m, centred on the outer corners (\u00b1105/\u00b1135, \u00b116), which matches the illustrated drawing at (-135.1,-16.1)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1/AC-4", "what": "Canyon rock and road", "value": "North-mass slant (-95,-44)->(-100,-30) against the table's (-100,-30.5): 0.5 m. South strip Z -22..-20 for X \u00b196: 0. North face built out to Z -48 (accepted ruling). Road strip 8.000 m wide (mitres recomputed at (-81.36,-30), (-68.36,-40), (-42,-40), (-27,-32) and their south partners). Midpoints of its 10 vertex pairs equal the table centreline exactly. Ends at X \u00b1102. Open at X 0", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1", "what": "Salt flat, fords, channels", "value": "Salt flat PlaneMesh 190x36 at (0,0.01,0): X \u00b195, Z \u00b118 (0). Fords X \u00b1(34..46), Z \u00b120 (0), zone 12x3x40 at y 1.5. Channel bodies X \u00b1(34..46), Z 20..48: 1.0 m past the table's 47 (accepted ruling)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1", "what": "Ridge", "value": "North edge Z 22, peak (0,21). Bevels (\u221395,22)->(\u2213100,32)->(\u221395,45.09) against the table's (\u221395,45): 0.09 m. Blocks X -100..-46, -34..34, 46..100. South side to Z 48 (accepted ruling). The bevel meets the A-1 outline at (-95.0,45.09): no ground route round it", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1/AC-8", "what": "Depot and the nine Fuel Can spots", "value": "Ring of 20 tangent dashes, all at r 9.000, y 0.02. Depot Cans (\u00b13,\u00b13) and (0,0); outer Cans (\u221388,-26) and (\u221362,14): all 0 m. Three fuel tanks r 2.5, 3 m tall, at r 8.000 (no collision), 1.26 m clear of the nearest Can", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1/AC-7", "what": "Cover positions, sizes and tilts", "value": "8 wrecks 6x3x1.3 at the table's positions. Yaws read from basis column 0: (-80,5) +30 (east end north), (-53,-8) -30 (south), (-22,-10) +20 (north), (-26,7.6) -45 (south); east four negated. Containers 12x2.5 (2 m tall) at (\u00b158,0), long axis X. Scrap walls 2.5x12 at (\u00b112,12), long axis Z. All 0 m", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-2", "what": "Mirror about X=0, read from the scene text (not executed)", "value": "Shore chain NW/NE and SW/SE pairs identical with x negated. The 5 cliff/ridge CSG polygons are symmetric vertex sets. Channels, fords, Cans and cover mirror, with wreck yaws negated. Base2 is Base1 turned \u00b190 degrees around a compound that is symmetric about the gate axis; the spares swap sides", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-3", "what": "Shore chain construction against the A-2 formula", "value": "32 separate StaticBody3D, layer 1, mask 0, no mesh, boxes 2.0 thick x 3.0 tall. Recomputed NW1, NW5, NW6 and SW6 (length L+e_a+e_b, centre, local X = t): match to under 1e-3 m", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-9", "what": "Floor and layers", "value": "One StaticBody3D, one BoxShape3D 300x1x100 at (0,-0.5,0), layer 1, no mesh. Cliffs and channels on layer 32 with mask 0; walls, legs, cover and shore on layer 1. Every drivable surface at y 0. Overlay heights 0.002/0.010/0.020/0.030, cast_shadow off on ground meshes", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-6", "what": "Gate and Garage lanes, judged from the geometry (runs not re-executed; D-1/D-2 measured them)", "value": "Gate 11.0 m. A Truck driving straight from a spare marker (x \u00b14) has 0.30 m to the gate edge, 0.50 m to the near leg and 0.80 m to the Garage side wall. Centre lane 0.50 m to the legs. Flag slot between the legs 3.4 m wide. The tank's lowest point (y 8) is above the camera (y 7)", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1", "what": "Own top-down snapshot of map_01.tscn (whole Map and both Bases)", "value": "Not taken: no shell tool in this session. The implementers' L3b/L3a/L2b captures were read instead and match the blueprint (bases, gate gaps \u00b15.5, Garage, tank, road bends, depot, cover, fords, channels)", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}], "checked": "This session had no shell tool (only Read/Glob/Grep/Write/Edit), so I ran no Godot or Python. I read every Map 01 scene in full: map_01.tscn, map_01_terrain.tscn, map_01_cliffs.tscn, map_01_water.tscn, compound_base.tscn, map_01_cover.tscn, map_01_depot.tscn and ford.tscn. I also read the material colours, base.gd, fuel_can.tscn, greybox_field.tscn (Sun and environment match it; shadow max distance 100), split_screen.tscn (Map is World's first child, field = %Map), the story's ACs and positions table, both drawings (blueprint px converted to metres: X=(px*1.32-120)/8-150, Z=(py*1.32-200)/8-50), and map_layout.gd. That scenario's POINTS, RECTS, EDGES and ROAD constants are the story's table, not copies of the build, so its check is not circular.\n\nI converted every transform by hand (Transform3D text is row-major) into world metres and compared it with the table, listing every deviation. None is over 1 m outside the accepted rulings: island A-1, rock and ridge to \u00b148, channels to 48, gate \u00b15.5. The mirror holds for every collider, zone, marker, seat and Can. Everything the blueprint draws is present, and the dashed rectangle, depot posts, Base containers and tyre stacks are correctly left to the look work.\n\nPlayability, judged from the geometry:\n- The long containers block the straight gate-axis line to the depot, as the blueprint intends.\n- The canyon road is the only ground route between the halves that avoids the fords; every salt-flat or sand-strip route crosses a ford's Z -20..20 span.\n- The road is 8 m everywhere; the Truck's 12.2 m turn radius was measured clean by B-5.\n- The raid needs a reverse (D-3; AC-6 wording allows it). The U-turn strip outside each gate is clear of cover and rock.\n\nNotes for the human playtest:\n- A Truck leaving from a spare marker has only 0.3 m to the gate edge. A player steering toward the gate centre from a spare clips the near tower leg (D-2: 16 of 24 aimed runs).\n- The depot's three 3 m tall tanks have no collision and sit in the approach lanes; the south one sits between the scrap walls. Units will drive through them, which may hide a Unit from its own camera (AC-13, look workflow).\n\nI wrote nothing to the repo, including no agent-memory files."}
