{"clean": false, "issues": [{"kind": "DESIGN", "file": "tools/evidence/split_screen/map_bases.gd", "quote": "const EXIT_END_Z: float = -30.0", "problem": "Binding correction D-2 counts an exit as done when the Unit's centre reaches Base-local z <= -40. base_exits stops at z -30 instead. The code comment explains why, and I confirmed it: a straight Truck lane from Base1's SpareSpawnRight (world z 4) first touches WreckWestOuterSouth at (-80, 5) when the Unit's centre is at local z -34.46, and Base2's mirror lane does the same. So D-2 cannot be met on Map 01 as built. The measured exit times are therefore to -30 (2.05 / 2.37 / 3.82 / 2.68 s), not D-2's times to -40 (2.48 / 2.88 / 4.77 / 3.32 s). AC-6 itself still holds: the Unit is 15 m past the gate's outer face and the corner towers end at local z -17.15.", "fix": "No code change. The orchestrator records in the Story 007 evidence doc that base_exits departs from D-2: it ends at Base-local z -30 because the wrecks at (+-80, 5) stand in the spare markers' lanes from local z -34.46, and it lists the times measured to -30."}, {"kind": "DEFECT", "file": "tools/evidence/split_screen/map_cover.gd", "quote": "_kit.need(problems, not cans.is_empty(), \"the Map has no Fuel Can under a Depot node\")", "problem": "_try_depot only checks that there is at least one Fuel Can under Depot, then drives past whichever Cans exist. Seeded defect M16 (FuelCanDepot3 deleted from map_01_depot.tscn, on the scratch copy) left cover_stops PASS. Only map_layout's map_positions caught it ('Fuel Cans 8 of 8'). AC-7's check of every depot Fuel Can therefore cannot fail on a missing Can, although DESIGN 5.8 names exactly five (FuelCanDepot1 to FuelCanDepot5).", "fix": "Make _try_depot require the five depot Cans that DESIGN 5.8 names. Either replace the non-empty test with a check that cans.size() equals a documented const DEPOT_CANS: int = 5, or look up FuelCanDepot1..5 by name and fail on any that is missing."}, {"kind": "UNVERIFIED", "file": "tools/evidence/split_screen/map_edges.gd", "quote": "const SHORE_AIMS: Dictionary[StringName, Vector2] = {&\"west\": Vector2(-141.55, -26.6),", "problem": "No driving run reaches the island's actual tips at (+-147, 0). The 'west' and 'east' shore runs aim at the north-west shoulder (-141.55, -26.6) and its mirror. A full-speed head-on run at a tip cannot be staged: the strip behind each Base's back wall is only 10 to 12 m deep, short of A-5's 15 m run-up. Static evidence covers the tips: the 32 shore boxes have inner faces 0.0000 m off the A-1 outline, overlap at least 0.25 m past every vertex and are 2.00 m thick. 672 shot-layer rays (mask 19) at y 0.1, 0.5 and 1.5 across every segment had 0 misses and hit 0.0000 m off the outline. Tip rays hit ShoreSW8 and ShoreSE8 at (-147, 0.5, 0) and (147, 0.5, 0). A-6 measured no tunnelling for walls from 0.02 m thick.", "fix": "No code change: AC-3 and DESIGN 6 name only the north, south, west and east shores and a channel, which map_edges covers, so adding a tip run would be SCOPE. The orchestrator records in the evidence doc that the tips are covered by the static ray sweep and the chain continuity numbers above."}], "measurements": [{"ac": "AC-1", "what": "My own probe compared the built positions with the POSITIONS TABLE (scratch copy, map_01.tscn instanced, 62 rows west and east)", "value": "SpawnPoint and spares (-125, 0 / -4 / 4), Flag seat and Flag (-113, 0), 9 Fuel Cans, 8 corner towers and 8 wrecks: 0.000 m off; wreck yaws -30 / 30 / 20 / -45 and mirrored: 0.00 deg off. Walls x -135..-105, z -16..16; Garage floor x -132..-122, z -6..6; delivery zone x -133.6..-106.1, z +-14.7; containers; scrap walls; fords; salt flat: all 0.000 m off. Tank 8 m across: 0.005 m. Gate z +-5.5 against +-5: 0.5 m (D-1). Channels z 20..48 against 47: 1.000 m (ruling, at the limit). Island against the table: 0.900 m; against A-1: 0.000 m. Canyon slant (-100, -30.5): 0.168 m. Ridge bevel (-95, 45): 0.032 m. Road centreline vertices 4.000 to 4.225 m from each edge (dev <= 0.225). Depot ring radius 9.000 (20 dashes). Sea plane +-500 m (>= +-162 x +-60). North face built out to z -48 (exempt). Scenario map_positions PASS (129 entries, extents max 1.000 m).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-2", "what": "Mirror about X = 0: world-space points of every collision shape (CSG faces from bake_collision_shape) with x negated, plus markers, Flag seats and Fuel Can spots", "value": "Probe: 99 shapes (76 layer-1 bodies, 1 floor, 2 layer-32 bodies, 5 layer-32 CSG, 15 areas), 0 unmatched, worst 0.0000 m, 5 symmetric about X = 0 themselves. 17 markers, seats and Can spots: worst 0.0000 m, headings 0.000 deg (Base1 faces +X, Base2 faces -X). Scenario map_mirror_data PASS (116 items, worst 0.0000).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-3", "what": "edge_shore: 4 types x north, south, west and east shores, plus channel runs; static check of the shore chain", "value": "16 shore runs stopped exactly at the half-length (1.30 / 1.50 / 2.20 / 1.20 m inside the outline), y 0.000, end speed 0.00, ray 0.000. Channel: Motorbike, Buggy and Truck stopped flush (pen <= 0.002 m); the Gyrocopter crossed the channel to the shore (1.21 m inside). Chain: 32 boxes, 2.00 m thick, layer 1, inner faces 0.0000 m off the outline, overhang >= 0.250 m. 672 rays: 0 misses. Byte-identical on two runs.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-3", "what": "Driving runs at the island tips (+-147, 0)", "value": "Not run (the strip behind the Base back wall is too short for a 15 m run-up). Static only: tip rays hit ShoreSW8 and ShoreSE8 at x = -147 and 147, and the chain is continuous.", "verdict": "NOT_VERIFIED"}, {"ac": "AC-4", "what": "edge_cliffs: canyon walls, ridge, canyon road both ways, shots; probe rays", "value": "Ground Units stop flush at the south canyon wall, the north slant and the ridge (pen <= 0.002 m); the Gyrocopter crosses each to the shore. Road runs with W held and no reverse, 0 contacts: Motorbike 8.86 s each way, Buggy 10.84 s, Truck 19.50 s (low speed 23.67 / 19.60 / 10.90). Shots end at (-14, -46.10) and (40, 46.03), past rock and water. Probe rays at y 0.5, mask 19: pass the south and north rock, the east rock, the ridge centre and west, and both channels; mask 32 sees each body. Shots are stopped by the container, a wreck, a scrap wall, a Base wall, a tower leg and the shore at both tips.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-5", "what": "ford_speed: each type across FordWest and FordEast", "value": "Held exactly 12.000 / 9.800 / 5.450 m/s (drive and measured speed) over windows of 61 / 74 / 134 ticks. The cap lifts +10 / +12 / +27 ticks after the centre leaves, consistent with G-4. Back to top speed +45 / +46 / +62; 24 / 19.6 / 10.9 at +64. Gyrocopter never capped (16.400). One shared resource at 0.50.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-6", "what": "base_exits, base_flag_run, first_spawn_problem", "value": "24 exits (4 types x 3 markers x 2 Bases), 0 wall-contact ticks; least gap Truck 0.300, Buggy 0.600, Gyrocopter 0.700, Motorbike 0.800 m (to local z -30, see the DESIGN issue). Flag run: the Round's own pick-up at local z -8.20 (seat -7.00, in the zone); a 27.60 m reverse was needed; delivered at Base1-local z -14.20; won after 18.22 s; carry_by() never called; refuel() added 12.50. first_spawn_problem() is empty for both Bases.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-7", "what": "cover_stops, plus probe rays at cover", "value": "12 runs at the wreck, container and scrap-wall twins (Gyrocopter and a ground type each) met the face at full speed, stopped within 1 tick, gap <= 0.003 m; 12 shots ended <= 0.000 m off the face. The Truck took all 5 depot Cans (1.38 s each). Every cover box is layer 1 with a collider.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-8", "what": "Nine Fuel Can spots, and reach on the spawn tank of 50 (Python model of unit.gd at 60 Hz: fuel burns first in the tick, move_toward at the acceleration, a ground Unit coasts when empty, the Gyrocopter is destroyed when empty; fords at half speed)", "value": "Spots (+-88, -26), (+-62, 14) and the depot five: all 0.000 m off. Open-ground reach: Motorbike 610.0 m / 27.0 s, Buggy 400.2 m / 22.0 s, Truck 185.1 m / 18.5 s, Gyrocopter 155.2 m / 10.0 s. Nearest Can (canyon west, about 59 m via the gate): all reach it (43.9 / 41.0 / 31.9 / 29.2 Fuel left). Nearest depot Can (about 122 m on the gate axis, through the west ford): all reach it (37.4 / 31.2 / 10.9 / 10.2 left). Opponent's Flag (about 238 m, both fords): Motorbike yes (26.4 left), Buggy yes (14.5 left), Truck NO (stranded at 162.8 m), Gyrocopter NO (destroyed at 155.2 m). With the depot Can's +40 on the way: all four reach it.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-9", "what": "Data in the Map, the floor, and the composition swap", "value": "TokenStock count_of: motorbike 5, buggy 3, truck 2, gyrocopter 2, unknown id 0 (token_stock.tres). The 2 Fords share one ford_settings.tres at 0.5 (layer 0, mask 2, monitoring on). Each Base owns 3 SpawnPoint markers; no PlayerStart or Player2Start. Floor: 1 shape, 300 x 1 x 100, layer 1, top y 0.000, x +-150, z +-50, under all rock, water and island extents (x +-149.01, z +-48.10). No collider under 1 m tall (no ramps). Scripts in the Map: map_field, ford, base, water_canister, fuel_can. Code outside the scene names no Map 01 path (split_screen.gd only retypes field to MapField).", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-9", "what": "dev07.py regress: 24 baselines on the greybox composition", "value": "ALL_OK=True. The strict twenty are byte-identical with exit 0; the soft four are RESULT ok and also byte-identical.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1..AC-7", "what": "Determinism: each of the five new scenarios run twice in the repo", "value": "map_layout, map_edges, map_ford, map_bases and map_cover each produced byte-identical output on both runs (sha eb91f1a9, 31b76492, 3e722a83, 76a4ee12, e7c73a84), exit 0, no ERROR or WARNING. The control copy matched the repo byte for byte.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "AC-1..AC-9", "what": "Seeded defects on a scratch copy (25 mutations, restored after each)", "value": "Every defect made at least one CHECK FAIL: M01 one shore box 0.3 m (edge_shore, map_mirror_data); M02 shore gap NW7+NE7 (edge_shore); M03 floor short of the channels (map_mirror_data, edge_shore, edge_cliffs); M04 south canyon wall without collision (edge_cliffs); M05 ridge on layer 1 (edge_cliffs); M06 channels on layer 1 (edge_shore, edge_cliffs); M07 fraction 1.0 (ford_speed, map_mirror_data); M08 Ford mask 18 (ford_speed); M09 cap never lapses (ford_speed); M10 leg in a lane (base_exits, map_mirror_data); M11 gate 6 m (base_exits, map_positions); M12 Garage side wall 1 m in (base_exits, map_mirror_data); M13 seat outside the zone (base_flag_run, map_positions); M14 zone shifted 5 m (map_positions; the bases checks pass); M15 wreck pair without colliders (cover_stops, map_mirror_data); M16 depot Can 3 missing (map_positions only, cover_stops PASS: see issue); M17 Base2 yaw 90 deg off (both map_layout checks, base_flag_run); M18 Motorbike 4 Tokens (map_mirror_data); M19 one Can moved 2 m (both map_layout checks); M19b both Cans moved 2 m, mirror kept (map_positions); M20 clamp while uncapped (ford_speed: 'lift never'); M21 delivery zones dead (base_flag_run); M22 containers on layer 32 (cover_stops); M23 north rock on layer 1 (edge_cliffs); M24 fraction 0.6 (ford_speed). After restoring, map_layout matched the repo.", "verdict": "PASS"}, {"ac": "STRUCTURE", "what": "Frozen files, assets, launch, MatchController, GarageQueue, Fuel Can scene, autoload, Timer, UI", "value": "All 9 frozen files OK. Assets unchanged. Main scene 120 frames and driving toy 60 frames: rc 0, no ERROR or WARNING. match_controller, garage_queue and fuel_can are not in the diff. No [autoload]. No Timer in the new gameplay files. No UI class referenced in changed gameplay lines.", "verdict": "PASS"}], "checked": "Map 01's layout half (AC-1 to AC-9) passes every headless measurement, but I am not reporting it clean: three minor issues remain.\n\n1. **Exit distance (DESIGN):** base_exits measures exits to Base-local z -30, not z -40 as binding correction D-2 says. A wreck at (\u00b180, 5) blocks the spare-marker lanes from local z -34.46, so D-2 cannot be met on this map. The orchestrator should record the deviation; no code change.\n2. **Depot check (DEFECT):** map_cover's depot pass only requires at least one Can. With FuelCanDepot3 deleted, cover_stops still passes; only map_positions fails. The fix is to require the five Cans that DESIGN 5.8 names.\n3. **Island tips (UNVERIFIED):** no Unit was driven into the tips at (\u00b1147, 0). The strip behind each Base is too short for a full-speed run-up. The static shore checks cover the tips.\n\n**Repo runs (read-only, one Godot process at a time):**\n- dev07 frozen: 9 of 9 OK.\n- dev07 assets: unchanged.\n- dev07 regress: ALL_OK. The strict twenty are byte-identical with exit 0, and the soft four end RESULT ok (also byte-identical).\n- The five new scenarios (map_layout, map_edges, map_ford, map_bases, map_cover) ran twice each: both runs were byte-identical, every CHECK passed, and nothing printed ERROR or WARNING.\n- dev07 launch: the main scene (120 frames) and the driving toy (60 frames) ran with no ERROR or WARNING.\n\n**Independent probe** (my own script, run on a scratch copy imported outside the repo):\n- **AC-1:** I checked 62 rows of positions-table entries. Everything is within 1 m. The largest offsets are the ones the rulings accept: the channels at 1.000 m, the island outline at 0.900 m, and the gate at 0.5 m.\n- **AC-2:** All 99 collision shapes mirror within 0.0000 m, with none unmatched. The 17 markers, Flag seats and Fuel Can spots also mirror within 0.0000 m with headings exact.\n- **Shore chain:**\n  - 32 boxes, each 2.00 m thick, with inner faces exactly on the corrected (A-1) outline and at least 0.25 m overlap past each corner.\n  - 672 shot rays across every shore segment: 0 misses.\n- **Shot rays:** shots pass through rock, ridge and channels and are stopped by cover, Base walls, tower legs and the shore at both tips.\n- **Data and floor:**\n  - Token stock reads 5, 3, 2, 2, and 0 for an unknown type.\n  - Both Fords share one settings file at 0.5.\n  - Each Base owns its own SpawnPoint markers, and first_spawn_problem() is empty for both.\n  - The floor is one layer-1 slab, 300 x 100 m with its top at y 0, under all rock and water.\n  - No ramps, and only the five expected scripts.\n  - Ground surfaces cast no shadows, and every mesh uses a shared material file.\n- **Structure:** MatchController, GarageQueue and the Fuel Can scene are unchanged; there is no autoload, no Timer and no UI reference in gameplay code.\n\nMy probe printed one FAIL (the road check), which was a flaw in the probe itself. I re-measured in Python: every road centreline point sits 4.000 to 4.225 m from each edge, so the road passes.\n\n**Seeded defects:** the five scenarios pass on an unmodified control copy. All 25 seeded defects (the 20 listed plus 5 extra) made at least one CHECK fail. The one weak spot is the missing depot Can in issue 2.\n\n**AC-8 fuel reach** (Python model of the unit.gd speed and fuel rules at 60 Hz, routes approximated, not an in-engine drive), for the evidence doc. On the spawn tank, open-ground reach is Motorbike 610 m, Buggy 400 m, Truck 185 m and Gyrocopter 155 m. All four reach the nearest Can and the depot. Only the Motorbike and the Buggy reach the opponent's Flag; the Truck and the Gyrocopter get there only with the depot Can's +40 Fuel picked up on the way.\n\nAC-10 to AC-15 (the look) were not checked; they are out of scope for this workflow. I wrote nothing in the repo.\n\nFiles are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/lens-ac-headless/:\n- lens_probe.gd\n- job1.py\n- job2.py\n- calc.py\n- job1.log\n- job2.log\n- probe.out\n- mut-details.txt\n- out/"}
