nd the soft four end RESULT ok (also identical).", "dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: map_layout 2 of 2 PASS (map_positions, map_mirror_data), map_edges 2 of 2 PASS (edge_shore, edge_cliffs; t=136.517), map_ford 1 of 1 PASS (ford_speed), map_bases 2 of 2 PASS (base_exits, base_flag_run), map_cover 1 of 1 PASS (cover_stops). Every RESULT ok, exit 0.", "No Godot process of mine is left running. The ps matches were my own zsh command line, whose echo text contains the word Godot."], "deviations": ["Issue 2: I also capitalised one more occurrence of the same convention that the issue's line list does not name. map_field.gd line 20: 'the flat field of stories 001 to 006' -> 'the flat field of Stories 001 to 006'. The code base writes the plural capitalised (unit.gd line 136: 'Stories 004 and 005'). Leaving it would keep map_field.gd mixing both forms, which is the problem the issue states. Same length, no rewrap."], "blockers": [], "summary": "Fix pass 1 (standards) is done: both issues are fixed. Only doc comments changed, so behaviour is unchanged, and every check passes, including the byte-identical baseline check.\n\n**Issue 1, ford.gd evidence pointer (fixed as proposed).**\nI confirmed the fix before applying it. The Story 006 evidence doc has no body_entered, monitoring or handler probe, only zone-listing latency. The Story 004 doc keeps both probes (rows 84 and 85), and fuel_can.gd cites Story 004 alone for the same sentence.\n- File: /Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/ford.gd, lines 24-25.\n- Before: `## and work done inside it cannot be ordered against a tick (the Story 004 and Story 006 evidence` / `## docs keep the probes).`\n- After: `## and work done inside it cannot be ordered against a tick (the Story 004 evidence doc keeps the` / `## probe).`\n\n**Issue 2, lower-case story references (fixed as proposed).**\nI capitalised \"Story\" in prose only; the production/epics/.../story-00N-*.md paths are unchanged. Every replacement keeps the same length, so no line was rewrapped.\n- /Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/map_field.gd:\n  - L10: 'the one story 004 set out' -> 'the one Story 004 set out'\n  - L12: 'typed GreyboxField until story 007' -> 'until Story 007'\n  - L21: 'written before story 007 keep' -> 'written before Story 007 keep'\n  - L40: 'Story 008 reads it; story 007 only holds it' -> 'Story 008 reads it; Story 007 only holds it'\n  - L20: 'stories 001 to 006' -> 'Stories 001 to 006'. This plural is the same convention but is not on the issue's line list; it is reported as a deviation.\n- /Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/maps/token_stock.gd:\n  - L13: 'story 007 only holds' -> 'Story 007 only holds'\n  - L15: 'is story 008's to enforce' -> 'is Story 008's to enforce'\n- /Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/src/gameplay/split_screen/split_screen.gd:\n  - L40: 'is story 008's to' -> 'is Story 008's to'\n  - L88: 'story 006 kept five greybox Cans' -> 'Story 006 kept five greybox Cans'. The issue names line 88, which reads 'story 006' rather than 004, 007 or 008.\n\nAfterwards no lower-case prose story reference remains in src.\n\n**Checks (all clean):**\n- import: no class changes.\n- parse: 14 files ok.\n- launch: both scenes start with no ERROR or WARNING.\n- frozen files: OK. assets/: unchanged.\n- lint007: 0 findings.\n- regress: ALL_OK, the strict twenty byte-identical and the soft four RESULT ok.\n- New scenarios: all five Map 01 scenarios pass with 8 of 8 CHECKs (map_layout 2, map_edges 2, map_ford 1, map_bases 2, map_cover 1).\n\nThe edit script stays in scratch at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/impl/fix1/apply_fix1.py. Nothing was written under tests/, docs/, design/ or production/, and nothing was committed.", "complete": true}
