{"files_created": [], "files_modified": ["/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_layout.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_edges.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_bases.gd", "/Users/tomas.kunzo/projects/ronin-ya/wasteland-fire/tools/evidence/split_screen/map_ford.gd"], "verification": ["Probe of the issue's proposed fix on Godot 4.7.2 (impl/fix1-tools/probe_const.gd): `const EDGES: Dictionary[String, PackedVector2Array]` with `PackedVector2Array([...])` values fails to load with 'Parse Error: Assigned value for constant \"EDGES\" isn't a constant expression.'", "Probe of a nested typed const (probe_nested.gd): `const EDGES: Dictionary[String, Array[Vector2]]` fails with 'Parse Error: Nested typed collections are not supported.'", "Probe of the form now in the file (probe_var.gd), using the exact text written: `var _edge_points: Dictionary[String, PackedVector2Array]` loads with no error and gives 3 keys, PackedVector2Array values and all 26 points", "Guard in the apply script (impl/fix1-tools/apply2.py): the table's 26 Vector2 entries and its 3 keys are textually identical before and after, in the same order. Every replaced doc block matched exactly once, and nothing was written unless every match held", "lint007.py all on the four files: functions over 40 lines or complexity ~10: 0; declarations without a ## line directly above: 0; ## lines over 100 columns: 0. Sizes: map_layout 349 -> 373, map_edges 452 -> 454, map_bases 295 -> 295, map_ford 281 -> 280", "dev07.py parse: ok on all 11 new or changed .gd files", "dev07.py import: rc 0, 233 classes, none new, none gone, no uid sidecars copied", "dev07.py launch: main scene 120 frames rc 0 noisy=[]; driving toy 60 frames rc 0 noisy=[]", "dev07.py new map_layout map_edges map_ford map_bases map_cover: every CHECK PASS and RESULT ok (2/2, 2/2, 1/1, 2/2, 1/1). The five full outputs are byte-identical (cmp) to a snapshot taken before the edits, including map_layout's 134 lines with its 129 SPLIT entries, so the EDGES change kept its behaviour", "dev07.py regress: ALL_OK=True. The strict twenty are identical with rc 0; the soft four end RESULT ok and are also identical", "dev07.py frozen: all nine frozen files OK; dev07.py assets: ASSETS UNCHANGED; git status lists the same files as at the start (no new repo files)", "grep after the fix: no 'preflight' or correction-letter (X-n) reference is left in map_edges.gd, map_bases.gd or map_ford.gd. The one measured number left in them, 'about 137' (map_edges.gd:32), carries '(the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run)' on the next line", "Scratch artefacts (probes, apply scripts, originals, before outputs, the unified diff fix1-tools.diff, verify.log) are under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tomas-kunzo-projects-ronin-ya-wasteland-fire/a0bbb76e-4a11-49a3-9a86-8984abd2268d/scratchpad/dev-story-007/impl/fix1-tools/"], "deviations": ["Issue 1 (EDGES): the proposed fix does not parse on Godot 4.7.2 (tested): a PackedVector2Array is never a constant expression, and nested typed collections are refused too. The right fix keeps the table typed by making it a private typed member var, `var _edge_points: Dictionary[String, PackedVector2Array]`. It moves from the const section to the head of the var section, keeping its 3-line doc plus one line saying why it is a var. The two lines in _edges() that read it are renamed (EDGES -> _edge_points), so the issue's statement that the consumer 'keeps working unchanged' does not hold for those two lines. Output is byte-identical.", "Size: map_layout.gd grows from 349 to 373 lines: 21 lines are the 14 docs issue 2 asks for, and 3 come from the table move and rewrap. This is above the 'about 350' of the TD-006 ruling, for the orchestrator to record. map_edges.gd grows from 452 to 454 lines (the rewrapped LIMITS doc and the pointer line).", "Issue 3 covered four same-kind references in map_edges.gd that the reviewer's line list did not name. All fall under the issue's stated problem: lines that point at scratch-only preflight corrections or give a measured number without the pointer. Line 45: '(A-5 asks 15; a Motorbike reaches 24 m/s in 14.4)' -> '(a Motorbike reaches 24 m/s in 14.4)'. Line 87: \"A-5's ray starts this far inside the outline (x) and ends\" -> \"A shore run's ray starts this far inside the outline (x), ends\". Line 313: \"A shore lane's A-5 ray\" -> \"A shore lane's ray\". Class doc lines 6-7: 'needs about 60 Fuel, a spawn gives 50' -> 'needs more Fuel than a spawn gives'.", "Finding, not fixed (outside the five issues, same standard): map_layout.gd line 13 '(preflight corrections A-1 and D-1 move entries by under 1 m)' and line 98, the doc above _edge_points, '(as the story's table had it, before preflight A-1)'. Also map_kit.gd lines 5-6 (\"the layout preflight's pursuit (B-5: ...)\"), line 17 ('(preflight B-5: at 10 m the Truck cuts corners)', a measurement), line 26 ('(preflight A-1 and A-3)'), line 70 ('(preflight A-1)') and line 185 ('(B-5)'). A later pass can apply the same rewording."], "blockers": [], "summary": "All five issues are fixed, in order. Only the four allowed scenario files under tools/evidence/split_screen/ were edited. Every check passed: regress ALL_OK, and the five Map 01 scenarios' full outputs are byte-identical to before the edits.\n\nISSUE 1 (map_layout.gd, bare Array inside the EDGES Dictionary):\n- The proposed fix does not work on Godot 4.7.2. I tested it: 'Assigned value for constant \"EDGES\" isn't a constant expression'. A nested typed const fails too: 'Nested typed collections are not supported'.\n- Before: `const EDGES: Dictionary[String, Array] = {\"Terrain/Island\": [Vector2(0, -46), ...], ...}` in the const section.\n- After: `var _edge_points: Dictionary[String, PackedVector2Array] = {\"Terrain/Island\": PackedVector2Array([Vector2(0, -46), ...]), ...}` at the head of the var section. It keeps its doc, plus '## A var, not a const: a PackedVector2Array is never a constant expression in GDScript.'\n- In _edges(), two lines change: `for paths: String in EDGES:` -> `for paths: String in _edge_points:`, and `for point: Vector2 in EDGES[paths]:` -> `for point: Vector2 in _edge_points[paths]:`.\n- The 26 points and 3 keys are textually identical and in the same order.\n\nISSUE 2 (map_layout.gd, 14 undocumented private functions):\n- Added a one- or two-line ## doc, at most 100 columns, above each of: _composition, _points, _rects, _edges, _landmarks, _mirror_data, _fords, _garages, _floor, _scripts, _xz, _box, _extent and _side.\n- Each doc says what the step checks and which AC it serves (AC-1 for the four position steps; AC-2 and AC-9 for the mirror step and the four data steps). Nothing else was added.\n- All 20 private functions now carry a doc.\n\nISSUE 3 (map_edges.gd), before -> after:\n- Lines 16-17: 'AC-3, AC-4 (preflight corrections A-1, A-2, A-5, B-1, B-5); design/rules.md' -> 'AC-3, AC-4; design/rules.md'.\n- Line 32: 'its runs take about 137.' -> 'its runs take about 137 (the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run).'\n- Line 42: '(preflight A-5)' dropped.\n- Line 45: '(A-5 asks 15; a Motorbike reaches 24 m/s in 14.4)' -> '(a Motorbike reaches 24 m/s in 14.4)'.\n- Line 48: '(preflight A-1);' dropped (outline;).\n- Line 67: '(B-5)' dropped.\n- Lines 78-84 (LIMITS doc): \"preflight A-5's unless named\" dropped; 'A-4 measured flush stops' -> 'where the stops are flush: the Story 007 evidence doc keeps the run'; the paragraph rewrapped.\n- Line 87: \"A-5's ray\" -> \"A shore run's ray\".\n- Lines 89 and 425: '(preflight A-2)' dropped.\n- Lines 241 and 370: '(B-5)' dropped.\n- Line 313: \"A shore lane's A-5 ray\" -> \"A shore lane's ray\".\n- Class doc lines 6-7: 'needs about 60 Fuel, a spawn gives 50' -> 'needs more Fuel than a spawn gives'.\n\nISSUE 4 (map_bases.gd), before -> after:\n- Lines 10-11: 'AC-6 (preflight D-1 to D-3,